A missing extended attribute is ENOATTR, and a filesystem without them has none.

MoneyMoney refused to start and showed its own FatalError.CodeSign message, that the application
file seems to be damaged and should be moved to the Trash. The bundle is intact: all 497 of its
sealed resources hash to what CodeResources says. What failed was the first thing the code-signing
machinery does with a bundle, an ordinary getxattr for com.apple.FinderInfo on the bundle root, and
our answer was EOPNOTSUPP.

Apple treats that as fatal. checkFork in libsecurity_utilities/unix++.cpp accepts ENOATTR and EPERM
and throws on anything else, so SecStaticCodeCreateWithPath came back as errSecErrnoBase plus 102
before a byte of the signature was read.

Linux and Darwin disagree here in a way the global errno table cannot settle, because the
disagreement is per call rather than per value: on Linux ENOATTR IS ENODATA, one number for both
"this stream has no data" and "this file has no such attribute", while Darwin splits them into
ENOATTR 93 and ENODATA 96. The table has to choose and chose ENODATA, which is right for the stream
calls and wrong for these. A filesystem with no extended attribute support answers ENOTSUP, and
macOS has no such filesystem, so no caller is written for that answer either.

So the six get, remove and list calls translate through their own helper: a missing attribute and an
unsupported filesystem both become ENOATTR, and a listing on such a filesystem is EMPTY rather than
an error. Setting one is deliberately left alone, because an application told its attribute was
stored when nothing was stored has been lied to.

Two plain bugs came out of the same reading. listxattr passed the GUEST path to the host syscall
instead of the expanded one, so every listing answered ENOENT for a file that plainly exists, while
getxattr beside it already used vc.path. And getxattr returned 0 rather than the length on success,
so a caller asking how big an attribute is saw an empty one every time; fgetxattr beside it already
returned the length.

MEASURED, on the MoneyMoney bundle: getxattr for com.apple.FinderInfo went from errno 102 to errno
93, listxattr from -1 ENOENT to 0, and SecStaticCodeCreateWithPath from 100102 to 0. LOOKED AT: the
application no longer shows the damaged alert and reaches its own startup screen with its logo,
toolbar and search field.

